From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: power-sequence the Zenbook A16's QCC2072

The A16's Wi-Fi is a QCC2072 (17cb:1112). Power-sequence it like the
WCN7850, and only descend into PCI bridge nodes when collecting PERST#, so
the wifi@0 node the device tree now describes is not taken for a port, as
Linux 7.4 does.
---
diff --git 1a/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-pwrseq.c 2b/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-pwrseq.c
index c5ced87..7a39c55 100644
--- 1a/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-pwrseq.c
+++ 2b/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-pwrseq.c
@@ -122,6 +122,11 @@ static const struct of_device_id pwrseq_pwrctrl_of_match[] = {
 		.compatible = "pci17cb,1107",
 		.data = &pwrseq_pwrctrl_qcom_wcn_pdata,
 	},
+	{
+		/* ATH12K in QCC2072 package. */
+		.compatible = "pci17cb,1112",
+		.data = &pwrseq_pwrctrl_qcom_wcn_pdata,
+	},
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, pwrseq_pwrctrl_of_match);
